// The set of names genia-2026's real reference host binds in its global
// environment (every `env.set`/`env.set_internal`/`env.register_autoload`
// call across `src/genia/builtins.py`, plus one more from
// `src/genia/interpreter.py`) -- generated by direct inspection of that
// authoritative source at the pinned contract revision (see
// protocol.hpp's `kContractRevision`), not guessed.
//
// Why this exists: E24-4's `deterministic_runtime_error_behavior`
// evidence (error-undefined-name.yaml) requires this host to normalize a
// genuinely undefined name to a specific `Error: Undefined name: <name>`
// diagnostic (see evaluator.hpp's `UndefinedNameError`). But this slice
// implements only a small fraction of genia-2026's real global names
// (print, map_*, utf8_encode, err, sum, map, apply_raw, ...) -- a
// reference to any OTHER real Genia name this slice has not yet
// implemented (e.g. `collect`, `sheet`, `map_item_key`) is genuinely
// BOUND in genia-2026's real environment, so claiming "Undefined name"
// for it would be flatly wrong, not merely unimplemented. The full
// shared-spec regression run (m0smith/genia-2026's tools.spec_runner
// against every case, not just this slice's pinned evidence) caught
// exactly this failure mode before this list existed: `true |> collect`
// and similar sources were producing a fabricated "Undefined name:
// collect" diagnostic instead of an honest "unsupported". This list is
// the fix: a name genuinely absent from BOTH this slice's own bindings
// AND this list is the only case honestly diagnosable as undefined;
// anything in this list but not yet implemented here must stay
// "unsupported" (see evaluator.hpp's Var-lookup handling).
//
// Regenerate if genia-2026's builtins.py changes (a one-liner, not a
// judgment call): grep -oE 'env.(set|set_internal|register_autoload)'
// against src/genia/builtins.py for the quoted first argument of each
// call, unioned and sorted.
